## 2. Crypto & Financial Policy Compliance (Avoid Instant Rejection)

Google Play enforces strict guidelines for **Cryptocurrency & Web3 apps**:

### A. Blockchain-Based Content Declaration
- In Google Play Console under **Policy > App content > Financial features & Blockchain**:
  - Declare that the app provides custodial/non-custodial cryptocurrency wallet services.
  - Comply with Google's Blockchain Content Policy: ICPay must **never** promote cloud mining or unauthorized token sales on device.

### B. App Access for Google Reviewers (Critical)
- Because Google reviewers must test the app, you must provide clear login instructions under **App content > App access**:
  - Provide a test Internet Identity / demo session instructions or test recovery seed so reviewers can log in without being blocked by hardware authentication.
  - Include a 1-minute YouTube demo link or screen recording demonstrating how funds and wallet features work.

### C. Permissions Declaration
- `app.json` includes:
  - `android.permission.USE_BIOMETRIC`
  - `android.permission.USE_FINGERPRINT`
- In Console, declare that biometrics are strictly utilized on-device for local app lock/unlock authentication.

### D. Privacy Policy & Data Safety Form
- **Privacy Policy URL**: `https://icpay.app/privacy`
- **Data Safety Form Answers**:
  - **Financial Info**: Account/Principal identifier (collected for app functionality).
  - **Personal Info**: Optional custom username handles.
  - **Data Encryption**: All data transmitted over secure HTTPS / IC replica protocol (TLS).
  - **Data Deletion**: Explain how users can clear their account/session from local storage or request username unlinking.

